ommand":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='.theseus/queue/in-progress/PKT-0021-characterize-the-remaining-pure-helpers-of-utils.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nlog=\"\"\"## Executor log\nTests added in `tests/unit/utils.tests.js` only; production code untouched. Surprising behaviors recorded (asserted as-is, not fixed):\n- `getJwtHsKey('')` returns a zero-length KeyObject (`symmetricKeySize` 0) instead of undefined: the empty string skips the `!res` cache guard's `!= null` check and `createSecretKey` accepts an empty buffer. An empty JWT secret therefore yields a usable HS key (security-relevant).\n- `getJwtHsKey` cache is keyed by `String(secret)`: a string and an equal Buffer collide, and whichever is cached first is returned for both.\n- `getJwtHsKey(123)` / `({})` swallow the error and return undefined.\n- `convertLicenseInfoToFileParams`: `users_expire` is NaN when the input is undefined (undefined / number).\n- `getContentDisposition` ignores the user agent argument and defaults to `attachment`.\n- `getBaseUrlByRequest` preserves the protocol case as given.\n- `getSecretByElem({string: ''})` returns undefined (empty string is falsy); file secrets are cached, so later disk changes are not seen; a missing file throws ENOENT.\n- `convertLicenseInfoToServerParams(undefined)` throws TypeError.\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"## Executor log\\n\",log,1)\ns=s.replace(\"## Spawned packets\\n\",\"\"\"## Spawned packets\n- Proposed (could not run `theseus packet new`, it needs approval): hardening packet \"Reject empty JWT secrets in getJwtHsKey/getSecretByElem\" (module common, type fix). It must also fix the string/Buffer cache-key collision. When it lands, update the characterization tests `getJwtHsKey: behavior for empty and non-string secrets` and `a string and an equal Buffer share one cache entry`.\n\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"test(common): record getJwtHsKey cache collision and log surprises for PKT-0021\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GfMVS4GJ2FBm26wB5X9Aot\" && git log --oneline | head -1"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":16,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've filled in the packet's Executor log, but I did not create the hardening packet for the empty JWT secret. `theseus packet new` needs approval in this run, so I listed it under \"Spawned packets\" as a proposal. It still needs to be created by someone who can run the command.\n\nBoth acceptance commands pass. `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` runs 608 tests (1 skipped) and `npx eslint tests/unit/utils.tests.js` is clean. I committed the work on the current branch.\n\n- **Test added:** I added one test, because the string/Buffer collision wasn't covered by the existing ones. It shows that `getJwtHsKey('collide-me')` and `getJwtHsKey(Buffer.from('collide-me'))` return the same cached key object. Only `tests/unit/utils.tests.js` changed in the code; production code is untouched.\n- **Packet edit:** The run rules say not to edit anything under `.theseus/queue/`, but the rejection feedback asked for the Executor log to be filled in. I edited only the Executor log and Spawned packets sections of the PKT-0021 file.\n- **Surprises recorded in the log:**\n  - `getJwtHsKey('')` returns a zero-length key instead of `undefined`, so an empty JWT secret gives a usable HS key.\n  - The key cache is keyed by `String(secret)`, so a string and an equal Buffer share one entry and the first one cached wins.\n  - `getJwtHsKey` returns `undefined` for a number or an object.\n  - `users_expire` is `NaN` when the input is `undefined`.\n  - `getContentDisposition` ignores the user agent.\n  - `getBaseUrlByRequest` keeps the protocol case as given.\n  - `getSecretByElem({string: ''})` returns `undefined`. File secrets are cached, so later disk changes aren't seen. A missing file throws `ENOENT`.\n  - `convertLicenseInfoToServerParams(undefined)` throws `TypeError`.\n- **Proposed hardening packet:** Reject empty JWT secrets in `getJwtHsKey` (module common, type fix). It should also fix the string/Buffer cache-key collision and then update the two `getJwtHsKey` tests that record today's behaviour.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- `getJwtHsKey` has a security-relevant gap: an empty secret yields a valid key.\n- Its cache is keyed by `String(secret)`, so a string and a Buffer with the same content collide.\n- I did not write these into the packet's \"Lessons for the Atlas\" section or the friction log.","ttft_ms":14435,"type":"result","duration_ms":66053,"uuid":"ba828f65-746b-4a16-8a48-afe8e2f80481","ttft_stream_ms":13954,"time_to_request_ms":354,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":197,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":2,"transcript_persist":17,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":32,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":7,"request_build":14},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":62,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":204,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":217,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":239,"process_anon_mib_result":148,"process_peak_rss_mib":256,"process_cpu_ms_turn":2261,"process_wall_ms_turn":66052,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":679,"process_wall_ms_strea